    rev_err_base:'Fill in the baseline above first (conversion rate, or mean and SD for a continuous metric).',
    rev_err_traffic:'Not enough traffic: with only {n} users per arm, even a very large lift would not be reliably detectable at these settings. Extend the test, add traffic, or relax α / power.',
    rev_res_n:'users per arm available (equal split)',
    rev_res_rel:'smallest detectable relative lift',
    rev_res_abs:'in absolute terms',
    rev_units:'units',
    rev_note:'Read it as: any true effect smaller than this will likely be invisible at your chosen power — the test can only reliably catch lifts at least this big.',
    rev_note_multi:'With {k} variants the per-comparison α is Bonferroni-adjusted (each variant vs control), which raises the bar — that is already included here.',
    an_skew_warn:'<strong>Small sample + heavily skewed data (n = {n}, skewness ≈ {sk}):</strong> with raw values this skewed and fewer than ~200 users per arm, the t-test may be fragile — a single extreme value can flip the result. Consider the <strong>Mann–Whitney U</strong> test, a log transform, or winsorising outliers (see Learn → When to check for normality).',
    btn_add_variant:'+ Add variant', btn_summary_stats:'enter summary stats instead',
